178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (SatQuery AI addresses three key technical risks in remote-sensing AI. Large satellite scenes are divided into small overlapping tiles to preserve spatial detail while keeping inference efficient. Differences in spectral characteristics across sensors, bands, and acquisition conditions are handled through multispectral/multimodal inputs and robust preprocessing. To reduce model overfitting, we use domain adaptation, regularization, early stopping, and cross-validation across diverse remote-sensing datasets. Together, these measures improve scalability, generalization, and reliability of the system across real-world satellite imagery.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Built with open-source AI, free EO data, and proven geospatial tools, SatQuery AI separates AI reasoning from deterministic measurement to deliver reproducible, auditable results. Its modular architecture supports deployment from a laptop to cloud-scale infrastructure without changing the core foundation.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
